{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>May He grant you grace, my son</b> — twice in the Masorah: here and the other: חנון יחנך לקול זעקך. This is what is in the Midrash: they asked him, How many sons do you have, and what are their names? He told him that for all of them he named them after the troubles that befell his brother. This is לקול זעקך — he told him that he was grieving over his brother; immediately his compassion was stirred and he said to him, Elohim grant you grace, my son."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:20.422485552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}